From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] A flip Xwayland completes as SUBOPTIMAL_COPY is not a copy

The pair rule (glx_stereo_pair.h, ORDER 561b: one copy tolerated, two take the
declaration back, three flips return it) reads the mode of a Present
completion: flipped when it is FLIP, copied otherwise. Xwayland completes a
flip as SUBOPTIMAL_COPY while a compositor's dmabuf feedback for the window's
surface is still unread (xwl_present_maybe_set_reason), and the surface of a
child window Stereo KWin has just redirected has fresh feedback: measured with
an Xwayland that prints its decisions, the first present of a declared child
was a flip completed as mode 3, and when the second one carried mode 3 too
(both feedback flags set) two flips took the declaration back and the window
went flat although both pictures had reached the surface. Mesa's own wsi code
already notes that Xwayland reports SUBOPTIMAL_COPY without any change to the
buffers (wsi_common_x11.c).

SUBOPTIMAL_COPY is now neither a copy nor a flip for the rule, on DRI3 and
software GLX, EGL on X11 and the Vulkan stereo layer: the completion is
ignored, as SKIP is. A copy that the server really made still completes as COPY
and is counted as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/src/vulkan/stereo-layer/stereo_layer.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/stereo-layer/stereo_layer.c
@@ -514,7 +514,10 @@
 static void
 x11_completed(struct swapchain_data *swapchain, int mode)
 {
-   if (mode < 0 || mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP)
+   /* Xwayland completes a flip as SUBOPTIMAL_COPY while the compositor's new dmabuf feedback is
+    * unread: the pixmap reached the surface, so it is neither a copy nor a confirmed flip */
+   if (mode < 0 || mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP ||
+       mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SUBOPTIMAL_COPY)
       return;
    struct surface_data *surface = swapchain->surface;
    xcb_window_t window = XCB_NONE;
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_x11.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_x11.c
@@ -103,7 +103,9 @@
 dri2_x11_pair_completed(struct dri2_egl_display *dpy, struct dri2_egl_surface *surf,
                         unsigned mode, int width, int height)
 {
-   if (!surf->x11_stereo_one_eye || mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP)
+   /* a flip Xwayland completes as SUBOPTIMAL_COPY is neither a copy nor a confirmed flip */
+   if (!surf->x11_stereo_one_eye || mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP ||
+       mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SUBOPTIMAL_COPY)
       return;
    xcb_get_geometry_reply_t *g = xcb_get_geometry_reply(dpy->conn,
       xcb_get_geometry(dpy->conn, surf->drawable), NULL);
--- a/src/glx/dri3_glx.c
+++ b/src/glx/dri3_glx.c
@@ -117,7 +117,10 @@
    if (!pdraw->base.stereo || !pdraw->base.dri_drawable ||
        !pdraw->base.dri_drawable->stereo_window_one_eye ||
        (!pdraw->stereo_declared && !pdraw->pair.flat) ||
-       mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP)
+       mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP ||
+       /* a flip Xwayland completes as SUBOPTIMAL_COPY (new dmabuf feedback unread) is
+        * neither a copy nor a confirmed flip */
+       mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SUBOPTIMAL_COPY)
       return;
 
    switch (glx_stereo_pair_completed(&pdraw->pair, pdraw->base.psc->dpy,
--- a/src/glx/drisw_glx.c
+++ b/src/glx/drisw_glx.c
@@ -229,7 +229,8 @@
          if (ce->kind == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_KIND_PIXMAP &&
              ce->serial == pdp->present_serial) {
             wait = false;
-            if (ce->mode != XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP) {
+            if (ce->mode != XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SKIP &&
+                ce->mode != XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_SUBOPTIMAL_COPY) {
                switch (glx_stereo_pair_completed(&pdp->pair, pdraw->psc->dpy,
                                                  pdraw->xDrawable,
                                                  ce->mode == XCB_PRESENT_COMPLETE_MODE_FLIP,
